WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.060
Welcome back to Tesla Short's Time Daily, Episode 464, it's May 6, 2026, and I'm Patrick

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:08.880
Inbankuver.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.340
Here's what's happening with Tesla today.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:19.680
Wadi-V ordered 370 Tesla semis in a roughly $100 million deal, the largest yet for the

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.340
electric truck.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.100
This marks the biggest semi-order Tesla has received so far.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:32.380
The agreement covers 370 trucks with the first 50 scheduled to arrive in 2026 and the

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.660
complete fleet in operation by the end of 2027.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.140
More than 300 of those units will handle a drainage work at the port of Oakland.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:47.320
They will be supported by new megawatt chargers capable of delivering roughly 300 miles of

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:48.900
range in about 30 minutes.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:55.220
The order indicates that fleet operators are moving past initial pilot programs and

00:00:55.220 --> 00:01:00.200
committing real capital now that the trucks and supporting charging infrastructure have

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.460
reached commercial scale.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:07.400
What stands out here is how quickly the economics are shifting for high utilization routes,

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.800
once charging speed and vehicle availability align.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:17.100
With this clear sign of electric trucking scaling in the real world, it is worth examining

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.040
how the overall approach changes the cost picture for operators.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:27.780
Wadi-V is pairing the trucks with dedicated high-speed chargers while also offering leasing

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.760
structures that reduce upfront capital exposure.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.860
That combination directly tackles the two main concerns for fleets logging high annual

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:42.660
miles, namely long refueling times and the risk of large equipment investments.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:49.360
By controlling the vehicles, the charging hardware and the financing in one integrated package,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:55.400
the operator can better predict total operating costs even before widespread public charging

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.120
networks are fully built out.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.700
Earlier deployments in Southern California ports have already shown millions of electric

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:08.860
miles accumulated, which gives some real world data on reliability under demanding conditions.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:14.960
If this model proves repeatable, it points to a practical path for battery electric trucks

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.120
in segments that were once considered too challenging for current technology.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:26.100
The same vertical integration could also help Tesla refine its own semi-production and support

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.140
systems as volume increases.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:34.160
While Tesla works through this hardware fix, it is simultaneously trying to lower the barrier

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.960
for new buyers with more flexible ways to get behind the wheel.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:45.420
Tesla is recalling more than 218,000 vehicles in the United States because the rear-view

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.440
camera feed can take too long to appear on the screen.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.860
The delay creates a potential safety concern when reversing, which is why the formal recall

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:55.640
was issued.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:02.420
Handling a recall this size will require careful coordination across mobile service teams and

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:05.360
clear communication with owners over the coming months.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:11.280
How quickly and transparently those fixes are completed could influence customer confidence

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:16.700
in both the current vehicles and Tesla's broader claims around future autonomy features.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:22.720
Service capacity will be tested, especially as the company continues expanding its mobile

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.120
fleet at the same time.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:30.460
Transparent updates on repair timelines and parts availability will matter a great deal

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.020
to owners waiting for the fix.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:38.340
Owners value clear information when issues arise, and steady execution here could help maintain

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.060
trust even amid the scale of the action.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:47.680
Tesla introduced five separate leasing tiers for the Model Y that let buyers match monthly

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.980
cost to the exact version they want.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:57.460
The entry point starts at $459 per month for the base rear wheel drive model, and rises

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:01.880
to $799 per month for the performance version.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:09.140
All options use standard 36 month terms with 10,000 miles per year, and modest amounts do

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:09.740
at signing.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:16.120
The structure reduces the need for large upfront cash while giving customers a built-in exit

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:21.040
after three years, when newer battery or hardware generations are expected.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:27.800
It directly addresses buyer hesitation about long-term ownership in a fast-moving technology

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:28.420
segment.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.640
By offering clear monthly pricing across the range, Tesla is making it easier for people

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.340
to step into a Model Y without committing to years of ownership.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:44.740
The same affordable Model Y that leasing is now pushing is already proving popular in price

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.100
sensitive markets abroad.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:54.580
The rear wheel drive Model Y sold 732 units in Hong Kong last month, taking the top spot

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.820
among all electric vehicles there.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:02.520
The result shows demand for the lower-priced variant remains strong in markets where price

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:06.920
sensitivity and local incentives favor more affordable trims.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:13.060
It also demonstrates that Tesla can still win volume segments even as competition broadens

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:13.940
across Asia.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:19.420
The rear wheel drive configuration appears to be hitting the right balance of cost and

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.640
capability for buyers in that region.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:27.320
Strong performance in a market like Hong Kong suggests the vehicle continues to resonate

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:31.760
where purchase incentives reward efficiency and lower price points.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:38.160
While Tesla defends its volume position in Asia, one rival is openly preparing a direct

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.940
challenge in the same segment.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:47.560
Lucid announced plans to launch a lower-priced electric vehicle in 2027, aimed squarely at

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:50.740
the Model Y and the upcoming Rivian R2.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:56.940
The move marks an attempt to enter the high-volume mid-range segment where Tesla currently holds

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.040
a strong position.

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:03.720
Execution will depend on lucid scaling production and cost structure quickly enough to compete

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:04.940
on price and range.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:10.400
The announcement highlights growing competitive pressure in the segment Tesla has led for

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.280
several years.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:18.020
Success for lucid will require not only competitive product specs but also reliable manufacturing

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:21.820
output at higher volumes than the company has achieved so far.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:28.460
On the social side, recent posts have shared a clear view inside the Tesla semi-cabin.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:35.040
The layout keeps the same minimalist approach as Tesla passenger cars, centered on a large

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.620
display and simple controls suited to long-haul driving.

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:44.960
It offers an early look at the daily environment for fleet drivers once volume production begins.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:51.160
Tesla also posted a reminder that its vehicles require very little routine service.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:56.420
Lower maintenance costs remain one of the clearest ownership advantages over internal

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:57.500
combustion vehicles.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.660
Especially for high-mileage fleet applications.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:07.720
The message reinforces a core part of the value proposition as more commercial buyers evaluate

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:15.540
the semi. An 11-year-old video of Elon Musk demonstrating the model SP90D acceleration to

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:20.480
Japan's former Prime Minister Shinzo Aiba has resurfaced this week.

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:26.280
The clip shows the instant torque and quiet cabin that surprised the visiting Prime Minister

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:32.660
and still draws strong reactions online. It captures an earlier era of Tesla when

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:35.980
performs demos help shift perceptions of electric cars.

